# Snippet Development Standards

**Source of truth:** for current snippets / render / LiquidDoc syntax/APIs query `shopify-dev-mcp` (`learn_shopify_api` → `search_docs_chunks`). This file covers only Foundation-specific conventions.

## Core Snippets Pattern (`@`-prefixed utilities)

**Core Snippets** are utility snippets prefixed with `@` (e.g. `snippets/@spacing-token.liquid`). They handle spacing, color, script injection, and other shared theme/customizer utilities. Modify them directly when needed, but when pulling updates from the foundation repo, manually sync changes to `snippets/@*.liquid`.

Category taxonomy (real snippets in this repo):

- **Spacing / layout**: `@spacing-padding`, `@spacing-token`, `@gap-token`, `@width-token`, `@height-token`, `@container-token`
- **Color**: `@color-scheme`, `@color-schemes`, `@system-colors`, `@text-color-class`
- **Scripts**: `@body-scripts`, `@needs-script`, `@track-recently-viewed`
- **Assets / utilities**: `@critical-css`, `@async-stylesheet`, `@preload-image-sizes`, `@text-alignment-classes`

## Documentation Requirement

Every snippet must open with a LiquidDoc `{% doc %}` block documenting each `@param` (with type and default) and an `@example` `{% render %}` call. This is mandatory, not optional.

## Testing-Scenario Comments

Include the relevant test cases in a comment so reviewers know what to exercise:

```liquid
{% comment %}
  Test cases:
  - Product with variants
  - Product without image
  - Product with compare_at_price
  - Out of stock product
{% endcomment %}
```

See [sections.mdc](sections.mdc) for the sections that render these utilities.
